course: dictionary
lesson: 14565
title: Pickled: food that lasts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pickled food has been kept in vinegar or salty water. This stops germs growing, so the food lasts a long time and tastes sour. «Mum bought a jar of pickled onions.» The clue is that pickled onions come in a jar, and the sour taste tells you they are kept in vinegar.
explain: Pickle can also be a verb, which is a doing word. To pickle food means to keep it in vinegar or salt water. «Gran pickles cucumbers every summer.» Gran is putting cucumbers into vinegar so they will last all winter.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The fish was pickled in vinegar so it would last all winter.» The words in vinegar and so it would last tell you what pickled means, even if you have never met the word before.
fact: Pickled can be an adjective (pickled onions) or a verb (to pickle food).
fact: Vinegar and salt stop germs growing, so pickled food lasts a long time.
fact: Before fridges, people pickled eggs, beetroot and cucumbers to keep them safe to eat.
fact: Pickled onions, pickled herring and pickled eggs are common examples.
fact: In old-fashioned slang, pickled can mean drunk, but that is a different meaning from the food one.
exercise: «Mum bought a jar of pickled onions.» What are pickled onions? | *Onions kept in vinegar so they last and taste sour | Onions wrapped in paper and frozen | Fresh onions picked from the garden that morning | Onions cooked in hot oil until crisp
exercise: «Gran pickles cucumbers every summer.» What does pickles mean here? | *To keep food in vinegar or salt water | To cook food on a hot grill | To wash vegetables under the tap | To pick fruit from a tree
exercise: «The fish was pickled in vinegar so it would last all winter.» Find and copy the word that means the fish was kept in vinegar. | *pickled | last | winter | fish
test: «Before fridges, people pickled eggs to make them last for months.» What does pickled mean here? | Dropped in cold water to wash them | Cooked in a hot pan | Painted in bright colours | *Kept in vinegar or salt so they last longer
test: Dad says, «The old man was pickled at the party.» In old-fashioned slang, what does pickled mean? | Cold | Hungry | Clean | *Drunk
exam: Why did people pickle food before fridges? | To make food look bright and new | To make food cook faster | To make food taste sweet | *To stop germs growing so food lasted longer
